{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 16 — NumPy fundamentals: arrays, vectorization, broadcasting\n","Objectives:\n","- Create ndarrays and understand dtypes/shapes.\n","- Vectorize operations to replace Python loops.\n","- Use broadcasting effectively."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import numpy as np\n","a = np.array([1,2,3], dtype=np.int64)\n","b = np.array([0.1,0.2,0.3], dtype=np.float64)\n","a.dtype, b.dtype, a.shape, b.shape\n","\n","# Vectorization vs loops\n","x = np.arange(1_000_000)\n","%timeit x * 2\n","\n","# Broadcasting\n","M = np.ones((3,3))\n","v = np.arange(3)\n","M + v\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Common operations\n","- Slicing, views vs copies.\n","- Aggregations and axis param.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["Z = np.arange(12).reshape(3,4)\n","Z, Z[:, 1:3], Z.sum(axis=0), Z.mean(axis=1)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Create a 1000x1000 matrix and compute row-wise means without loops.\n","2) Normalize each column to 0-1 range with broadcasting.\n","3) Demonstrate the difference between view and copy when slicing."]}]}
